the latest hero to receive the medal of  honor faces a harrowing personal battle  at home  president Trump awarded the highest  military honor yesterday to former Army  Staff Sergeant Ronald Shore for his  bravery in Afghanistan David Martin  shows us what the sergeant faced in the  war zone and the struggle he's dealing  with now the team of Green Berets and  Afghan commandos went in by helicopter  to capture or kill suspected Afghan  terrorist leaders but for Staff Sergeant  Ronald sure that day in the spring of  2008 became a five-hour battle to save  the lives of his own men firming person  I just became a a mission of just  getting as many guys out of there as I  could the enemy held the high ground and  the Green Berets were under withering  fire sure was the team's medic Ron raced  to each patient giving them life-saving  care they were bleeding profusely I  heard the first calls for medic and at  that point worked my way over to the  first person did you have to expose  yourself to fire to get there yes I mean  I get there did you get it I know when I  was shot in the helmet and what are you  okay felt like somebody hit me and the  helmet with a baseball bat  well Apache helicopters rocketed the  village and jets dropped bombs within  danger close range sure kept moving  across open ground to treat the wounded  medevacs braved the firestorm to  evacuate the casually sure had treated  not a single American died in that  brutal battle thanks in great measure to  Ron's heroic actions sure got out of the  army and joined the Secret Service when  the president told him he would be  receiving the Medal of Honor what he  said out of Honor I was so confused that  I really don't remember what else he  said confused why confused to be singled  out it all just  just doesn't make sense there's one  other thing about 39 year-old Ronald  sure that won't make sense to anyone  that's diagnosed with lung cancer last  year what's the prognosis taking it one  day at a time he's faced death before  and knows exactly what he has to do  we're just giving this fight everything  we can just just like the last one for  CBS this morning David Martin in  Washington
 

